{
  "$comment": "Single source of truth for material identity, shared by JS and C++. Edit here, then run `npm run generate` to regenerate materials.generated.js and cpp/engine/materials.generated.hpp. Numeric ids MUST stay stable: saved scenes, worldgen, tests, and the WASM grid key off them. `materialClass` is the broad gameplay/physics bucket and `flags` add cross-cutting traits, so a new material that reuses existing physics needs only a schema entry.",
  "tableSize": 256,
  "kinds": {
    "NONE": 0,
    "POWDER": 1,
    "LIQUID": 2,
    "GAS": 3,
    "COMPONENT": 4,
    "FREE_RIGID": 5
  },
  "$placementProfileDoc": "Generic placement policy is explicit per material kind. paint writes loose cells; structure enters the component/body-aware placement path; erase clears cells. Add a new kind here and in kindPlacementProfiles before any material can use it.",
